data/
# .git/ stays excluded even though the build has to read it. hatch-vcs derives
# the package version from the repo's tags, so the final `uv sync` can't build
# this project without that metadata -- but it arrives as a *named build context*
# (compose.yml's `additional_contexts: gitdir: ./.git`), which is a separate
# context this file does not filter. Keeping the exclusion is the point: a future
# stray `COPY . .` can never bake the full history, and whatever was ever
# committed and later removed from it, into an image layer.
.git/
sdk/
tests/
*.log
*_out.ipynb
